# L §3.3 periodic: "A power that isn't an integer needs to u": the effective rate of 12 %/year per month is
# 1.12^(1/12) - 1. The period is in the rate's value, so the check is the run's, made where the value is read, in
# load's words: RUN-DOMAIN (L §8.4 Load refuses what load sees; tally 2.1.8 §4, #162). 2.1.7's refcore printed LOAD-TO
# at run, refusing the reality.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input r: rate
def p: num = periodic(r, month, effective) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 12 %/year

ask a: p law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: refused: RUN-DOMAIN periodic needs to u
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
